        "text": "Answers\n1.\nFalse. Generative AI models can take text as well as image, video, and audio data as inputs.\n2.\nVAEs, GANs, and autoregressive models.\n3.\nDeepfakes, misinformation, issues with copyright or intellectual property, and job displacements\nare some of the social and ethical implications of generative AI.\n4.\nSome of the common methods to address bias in training data are oversampling or undersampling.\n5.\nMistral, LLaMA, and Bloom are some of the open source text and content generation LLMs.",
